counterfactuals.output:
A method performed by a mobile computing device, comprising:

executing a first application on the mobile computing device;

determining, by the first application, that a user has completed a predetermined task;

in response to determining that the user has completed the predetermined task, generating, by the first application, reward information corresponding to a reward to be provided to the user;

initiating, by the first application, execution of a second application on the mobile computing device; and

transmitting the reward information from the first application to the second application locally on the mobile computing device,

wherein the transmitting is performed without communicating the reward information to a backend server.

In some embodiments, the reward information comprises at least one of a reward identifier, reward amount, reward type, expiration time, user identifier, task identifier, or validation token. The first application may initiate the second application using an inter-application communication mechanism, including a deep link, custom uniform resource identifier scheme, app intent, operating system intent, shared local storage, pasteboard, or local application programming interface. The second application may receive the reward information and perform at least one of displaying the reward, storing the reward, validating the reward, or applying the reward to an account, transaction, or in-application benefit.

A system may include a mobile computing device comprising one or more processors and memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the mobile computing device to perform the foregoing method.

A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium may store instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a mobile computing device, cause the mobile computing device to execute the foregoing operations.
